'''Attribute Fusion''' is the process of combining different [[Attributes|Attribute Shards]] to obtain new Shards. This process can be done in the {{Zone|Fusion House}} in {{Zone|Tangleburg}}, or remotely with {{NPCSprite|Kysha}}'s [[Abiphones|Abiphone Contact]].

== Usage ==
Interacting with the '''Fusion Machine''' opens a menu which lets you select the Shards you wish to fuse. Once two Shards are selected, a list of Shards that you can obtain upon fusing your selection is displayed.

{{/UI}}

The number of Attribute Shards needed for fusion depends on the initial input:
* {{Item|Chameleon Shard|text=Chameleon}} requires {{Green|1}} Shard
* '''Reptile''', '''Amphibian''' and '''Elemental''' Shards (e.g. {{Item|Gecko Shard|text=Gecko}}, {{Item|Eel Shard|text=Eel}}, {{Item|Mossybit Shard|text=Mossybit}}, {{Item|Bolt Shard|text=Bolt}}, etc.) require {{Green|2}} Shards
* In all other cases, {{Green|5}} Shards are required

The number of Attribute Shards outputted during fusion depends on the type of fusion.
* '''ID Fusion''' and '''Chameleon Fusion''' yield {{Green|1}} Shard
* '''Special Fusion''' yields {{Green|2}} Shards
* Using any '''Reptile'''-type Attribute Shard, including {{Item|Chameleon Shard}}s, has a chance to activate the {{Attr|Pure Reptile}} Attribute which grants a {{Green|2%}}-{{Green|20%}} chance to double output shards during a fusion.

== Fusion Recipes ==
{{See also|Attributes#List of Attributes}}

Inputting {{Green|2}} Attribute Shards together will output a maximum of {{Green|3}} new Shards: only one output can be selected with each fusion. There are {{Green|3}} 'types' of Fusion: each type will yield different outputs, and they are outlined below. Fusion recipes can never output one of their inputs.

== Fusion Types ==
=== ID Fusion ===
'''ID Fusion''' recipes function sequentially. Each Shard has a pre-defined "ID result". It typically follows a pattern of having the same category and rarity of the Shard. Then, an algorithm is used to determine the results from ID Fusion.

Pseudocode:<ref name="idfusion" />

 '''if''' shard1's category = shard2's category '''then'''
    '''if''' shard1's rarity = shard2's rarity '''then'''
        '''if''' shard2's id result = shard1 '''then'''
            id result = shard1's id result
        '''else'''
            id result = shard2's id result
    '''else'''
        id result = higher rarity shard's id result
 '''else'''
     id results = shard1's id result, shard2's id result

=== Special Fusion ===
'''Special Fusion''' recipes consist of pre-defined recipes that output a specific Attribute Shard. Special Fusion recipes generally follow a specific thematic pattern depending on the family and rarity of the input Shards.

=== Chameleon Fusion ===
'''Chameleon Fusion''' is a special type of '''Fusion''' that only works with a {{Item|Chameleon Shard}}. Fusing with a {{Item|Chameleon Shard}} is guaranteed to output the next {{Green|3}} eligible IDs of the Shard of the other input, even if any of the given Shards outputted are not regularly obtainable from fusion (e.g. {{Item|Gecko Shard}}) with the exceptions of these shards:
*{{Item|Bitbug Shard}}
*{{Item|Doomspiral Shard}}
*{{Item|Macaw Shard}}
*{{Item|Shinyfish Shard}}
*{{Item|Galaxy Fish Shard}}
*{{Item|Molthorn Shard}}
*{{Item|Starborn Shard}}
*{{Item|Primordial Shard}}
*{{Item|Rainbug Shard}}
*{{Item|Timestalk Clone Shard}}
*{{Item|Wumpa Shard}}
Only one {{Item|Chameleon Shard}} is required for the input, and only one Shard will be outputted.

If no correct shard is found, the first shards of the next rarity will be outputted (for example: {{Green|R63}} + {{Item|Chameleon Shard}} will result in {{Green|R64}}, {{Green|E1}} and {{Green|E2}}). Legendary rarity shards are the exception; if no correct shard is found, the output slot will be empty.

